{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Key evidence: multimodal multiprofile with avgpool+concat (config_002, acc=0.632) underperforms RNA-only multiprofile (config_050 avgpool=0.650, config_044 transformer=0.653), which is counterintuitive. In the RNA-only setting, transformer aggregation gave a small but consistent edge over avgpool (0.653 vs 0.650). Config_018 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings identical to config_002 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat). This clean single-variable comparison directly tests whether the aggregation mechanism—which we know matters for RNA profiles—also rescues the multimodal model's underperformance relative to RNA-only. If transformer aggregation closes or narrows the gap, it implicates profile aggregation as the bottleneck; if not, the issue lies in fusion or image-feature quality, guiding subsequent experiments toward weighted fusion or alternative image encoders. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information next step because it isolates one design axis with existing supporting evidence rather than introducing multiple simultaneous changes."
}

